# Image Optimization & Performance Plan

Address site sluggishness and heavy memory consumption caused by massive print-resolution image assets in `src/imports/`.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The portfolio was bundling over 220 MB of uncompressed print-ready artwork on a single page. `Adom Beauty` alone was 64.2 MB and 432 megapixels (15,000 × 28,800 px).
>
> All oversized assets have been downscaled to crisp web-standard high-definition dimensions (maximum 2400px at 82% JPEG quality), dropping total payload by over 95%.

## Proposed Changes

### Image Optimization Script

- Run an optimization script using `sharp` targeting all images in `src/imports/` over 1MB.
- Resize images exceeding 2400px on their longest edge down to a maximum of 2400px while maintaining aspect ratio.
- Re-encode with progressive JPEG / Web compression at 82% quality.
- Keep exact same filenames and paths so zero imports or links break.

### Frontend Optimization

#### [GraphicDesign.tsx](file:///c:/Users/ernes/Desktop/Digital%20Portfolio%20Builder/src/app/pages/GraphicDesign.tsx)

- Add `loading="lazy"` and `decoding="async"` attributes to thumbnail image elements.
- This ensures off-screen portfolio items are only loaded and decoded into memory when scrolled into view.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification

- Run `npm run build` to verify that all assets bundle cleanly and output size is drastically reduced.
- Measure total bundle size reduction.

### Manual Verification

- Verify that portfolio cards and lightbox preview render cleanly and sharply without lag or memory hitching.
